V4 hybrid inference-state memory: Qwen3.5 GPU passes without copying the cache. Qwen3.5-4B-Q8 INT8 on the RTX 5050 laptop GPU (8 GB,
40 W, ~0.75 GB held by the desktop), release builds, GPU idle and <= 52 C before each run. "Before" is the tree at commit 25954df built
separately; "after" is this tree. Harness: 18-harness/.

1. Audit of every path that writes Qwen3.5 GPU cache state (crates/model/src/qwen35)
   path                          what it writes                                        undo before                    undo now
   forward: decode / prefill      DeltaNet conv+recurrent (kernels, in place); keys and  stage(): full clone of both,   mark of the DeltaNet state (53 MB) +
   (one call, chunks of 512)      values at rows [len, len+n) and new pages; ledger     swapped in on success          cut keys and values back to the old length
   sliced prefill (64 tokens)     same, once per slice                                   one full clone per slice       one mark per slice
   batched decode (1-4 caches)    same, in place for every cache in the batch           none; failure marks every      unchanged: failure marks every cache
                                                                                         cache for replay               for replay (each one independently)
   truncate / clear               ledger, replay flag                                    replay flag                    unchanged, and bumps the cache's epoch so marks die
   replay pass                    zeroed state, whole history                            fresh cache allocated          state and keys/values reset in place
   chat boundary (Session)        a second copy of the cache (state + all KV)            full clone, swapped back      Mark + rewind: no copy of keys and values
   server retained session,       an independent cache that outlives the request         full clone                     unchanged (needs a real copy)
   shared prefix
   disk checkpoint import/export  new cache filled block by block                       n/a                            unchanged
   Keys and values are append-only: kv_store writes at the committed length, only advance() commits, and every cache owns its slabs, so
   there is no aliasing. A failed pass can leave rows past the committed length written and pages mapped; truncating to the old length
   frees the pages and the rows are overwritten by the next write. Only the DeltaNet state is mutated in place.

2. Gates, fixed before implementation
   C1  every existing transactional / rollback / batch / prefix / checkpoint test passes unchanged; a failure after partial writes leaves
       every committed byte as it was; mark/rewind is bit-exact; HF verification unchanged.      C2  greedy chat and code output identical to before.
   M1  process VRAM peak at 8k and 14k down by about one KV copy (>= 0.4 / 0.8 GB).   M2  the planner's estimate is not below the measured
       peak and admitted context rises only as far as the measured saving allows (512 MiB safety kept).
   P1  decode at 128 tokens within 2%.   P2  decode at 8k up >= 20% and at 14k up >= 35%.   P3  prefill and first token within 3%.
   P4  no replay cliff inside the newly admitted window (a chat of >= 24k tokens reuses every turn).
   O1  `reused` counts only tokens a cache did not read again; a forced replay is reported with a reason.

3. Results (matched, interleaved before/after; 18-harness/ab_before_after.sh; decode tok/s, p50 ms, process VRAM peak by nvidia-smi pid)
     128 in/64 out  (3 pairs, 3 runs + warmup)   before 40.12 / 39.80 / 40.01 (24.5-24.9 ms)    after 40.09 / 40.31 / 40.29 (24.2-24.6 ms)    4,472 -> 4,376 MiB
     2,048 in/33 out                              before 36.67 (27.18 ms)                          after 39.43 (25.18 ms)                          4,696 -> 4,568
     8,192 in/33 out                              before 27.18 (36.20 ms)                          after 35.34 (27.30 ms)                          5,496 -> 4,984
    14,336 in/33 out                              before 22.27 (44.90 ms)                          after 31.98 (31.53 ms)                          6,296 -> 5,368
   prefill: 135.6/134.3/134.6 -> 134.2/135.1/134.6 (128), 127.3 -> 127.4 (2k), 100.7 -> 98.8 (8k), 75.3 -> 76.8 tok/s (14k); first token 944-953 ms -> 947-954 ms (128),
   16.09 -> 16.07 s, 81.4 -> 82.9 s, 190.5 -> 186.7 s. Profile (marin-run bench --profile, 17 tokens): "state transaction copy" per decode token
   was 10.0 ms at 8k (28%); it is now 0.48 / 0.56 / 0.59 / 0.54 ms at 128 / 2k / 8k / 14k (<= 2.3%). Decode at 8k 36.3 -> 28.0 ms/token.
   Gates: P1 pass (40.0 -> 40.2), P2 pass (+30% at 8k, +44% at 14k), P3 pass, M1 pass (-0.5 GB at 8k, -0.93 GB at 14k).

4. Long chat, ctx 28672, 1,400-token turns, 8-token replies, greedy (18-harness/long_chat.rs.txt): 19 turns up to 27,143 tokens; every turn
   reused everything but its new ~1,460 tokens (replayed 0); wall 11.1 s (turn 1) ... 21.6 s (turn 10, 14k) ... 42.9 s (turn 19, 27k); process
   VRAM 4,568 MiB (turn 1) -> 6,232 MiB (turn 19), +~96 MiB per turn = one KV copy (before: +~288 per turn). Before, the same chat at ctx 15360 ran turns 1-7 in
   11-17 s, then turn 8 123.2 s, turn 9 155.0 s, turn 10 180.3 s (full replays, 17-harness). P4 pass.

5. Planner (marin plan, GPU budget "full window", decimal GB; process peaks above are MiB; free VRAM 7.17-7.26 GB, it moves with the desktop)
     ctx      before            after             measured process peak after (bench)
     2,048    4.92 GB (4,692)   4.84 GB (4,616)   4,568 MiB   (+48 MiB margin)
     8,192    5.74 GB (5,474)   5.26 GB (5,016)   4,984       (+32)
    14,336    6.56 GB (6,256)   5.67 GB (5,407)   5,368       (+39)       before: planner 6,256 vs measured 6,296 (40 MiB under)
    28,672    -                 6.64 GB (6,333)   6,328 extrapolated from 6,232 at 27,143 tokens (+5)
   Admitted context: before max 15,360 (16,384 refused: needs 7,366 MB, 7,247 free); after 26,624 accepted, 28,672 accepted at 7,257 MB free and refused at
   7,170 MB free (needs 7,177), 32,768 refused (needs 7,454). The estimate sits within 5-50 MiB of what was measured and the 512 MiB safety is unchanged.
   The mark rule is the same safety rule as before: a mark needs its 53 MB plus the 512 MiB slack free, otherwise none is taken and the next turn
   reports a replay.

6. Server (marin serve --ctx 8192; 2 concurrent ~5,000-token prompts; 18-harness/server_two_requests.sh)
   before: "up to 1 at once": request 1 ok in 41.7 s, request 2 refused after the 10 s queue limit ("request waited too long", 408).
   after:  "up to 2 at once": both ok (200) in 80.7 and 82.0 s; server process VRAM peak 5,176 MiB in both runs (before one request at 5,176).
   max_active now reserves one idle session copy instead of two (the second was the staged copy of a pass). ctx 4096 stays 3, ctx 12288 stays 1.
   The server's retained session and shared prefix are still full copies (checkpoint_cache), as they must be independent caches.

7. Correctness (C1, C2)
   - crates/model/src/qwen35/gpu_tests.rs gpu_sessions_replay_reset_and_late_failure_are_transactional passes unchanged on the tiny fixtures and the
     real 4B-Q8 (state and keys/values bytes equal after a failed pass; replay, reset, checkpoint copy, batch failure).
   - gpu_mark_tests.rs (new): a failure injected after 0, 2, L, L+1 and 2L-1 layers of a 700-token (two-chunk) pass leaves every committed byte, the
     ledger and the length as they were, no replay flag, and the retry equals the twin bit for bit; a failing replay pass stays a replay and then
     succeeds; a mark returns the cache bit-exactly after 600+ appended tokens and the next token equals the twin's; a mark is refused after a
     cut-back, a restart or on another cache.
   - runtime replay_tests.rs: reused / replayed accounting for a cache that cuts back in place and one that cannot.
   - cli chat_marks.rs (tiny Qwen3.5 on the GPU): 5 turns reuse the previous body with replayed 0; a new conversation reports replayed > 0 and reused 0;
     the turn after is marked again. chat_reuse (real 4B, cancel during prefill) and checkpoint tests unchanged.
   - Greedy chat (6 turns, 4B-Q8) and code-mode answers (2 questions with tools) are byte-identical before and after.
   - Focused suites on the tree before the final run: model + runtime + cuda 194 passed, cli 455 passed, 0 failed.

8. Observability (O1): Outcome gains `replayed`; `reused` = tokens kept and not read again. runtime::SequenceCache::replays() lets generate see that a cut-back
   forced a replay (Qwen3.5 GPU and CPU caches). Session::prefill reads such a start from the beginning in 64-token slices, so Ctrl-C is heard. The inspect
   panel and /metrics print "replayed N tokens (this model's state cannot be cut back to a shared start, so they were read again)"; no prompt text is shown.
   Also: a conversation that outgrows the window drops its oldest turns, the prompt no longer starts like the cache, and that is now reported as replayed.

9. Low VRAM (18-harness/ballast.rs.txt holds GPU memory; long_chat.rs.txt pauses after turn 3): 230-token turns, ctx 2048; after turn 3 another process takes
   all but 280 MiB of free VRAM (2,137 MiB held). Turns 1-3: reused 0/264/513, replayed 0, 2.1 s each. Turn 4: no mark could be taken (needs 53 MB plus
   the 512 MiB slack), the cache keeps prompt+reply (1,025 tokens). Turns 5-8: reused 0, replayed 1,014 / 1,263 / 1,512 / 1,761, 9.6 / 11.5 / 13.4 / 15.4 s;
   no OOM, no crash, the conversation continues, and every replay is reported. (The mark rule is unchanged: free >= mark bytes + 512 MiB.)
   A load with 1.9 GB held up front is refused by admission before anything starts; with 1.0-1.5 GB held, turns behave as without ballast.

10. Not done / limits: marks are single use and tied to one cache and epoch; the server and shared-prefix copies are still O(window); CPU Qwen3.5 passes are
   unchanged; the planner margin at the largest context is ~5 MiB over the measured extrapolation (the 512 MiB safety is what covers it);
   if the mark cannot be taken for lack of VRAM the next turn replays (reported).
